00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:31,760
And so we were able to quickly say, let's rip this out because the data is reliable.

414
00:39:31,840 --> 00:39:32,240
It's working.

415
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:32,960
Like we're doing.

416
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:34,160
You have it under control.

417
00:39:34,400 --> 00:39:38,080
And if you have the right people who understand it to respond to, like, enhancements.ement requests and stuff like that.

418
00:39:38,400 --> 00:39:40,000
I think it can be very superior.

419
00:39:40,240 --> 00:39:48,880
But like on the cost point, it's like if your product generates any revenue like marginally per user, usually the like tracking and analytics stuff is a rounding air.

420
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:59,120
I mean, when it's a rounding air, you know, when you're talking about like billions of events a day, for example, versus like we were in like another level on that.

421
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:04,320
But like I think that if Disney Plus had launched incredibly slowly or Yeah, or wasn't it?

422
00:40:04,640 --> 00:40:08,960
Or anything like any SPN Plus, I don't think that we even had Adobe integrated there.

423
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:09,600
Maybe we did.

424
00:40:09,920 --> 00:40:12,560
But like in that case, it would have been fine to run that and not have to.

