00:40:58,880 --> 00:41:04,160
Well, that's, I think, one of the, you know, locking into a tool stack that has constraints like that.

440
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:08,320
I think it forces you to not do things that might be helpful because of the cost.

441
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:09,520
And that stinks.

442
00:41:09,680 --> 00:41:18,880
Like, because sometimes if you really want to do something and you're like, oh, I can't because MixPanel or whoever is going to charge me a hand and a leg, then like, you know, which you also run into with your own stack sometimes.

443
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:24,560
But again, it's like sometimes you can just bring events into the first stage of your processing and leave them there.

444
00:41:24,720 --> 00:41:29,920
Like, you're like, we might even not pull these into Snowflake yet, but we're just going to let them stack up in cold storage.

445
00:41:30,080 --> 00:41:31,520
And like, if we ever need them, we have them.

446
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:33,280
You can make those decisions, right?

447
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,880
And control costs quite effectively.

448
00:41:35,280 --> 00:41:49,920
It goes back to the original kind of question and statement, which is that having those checkpoints or evaluation points understood across the business and the teams, and then adhering to them, can actually prevent a lot of what seems like a risk, right?

449
00:41:50,240 --> 00:42:06,080
You could say, we're going to have Adobe in here, but if we're moderately successful, we need to evaluate within three months whether or not the continued cost needs to start being offset, whether or not it's theres that we're scaling back some of the events or whether or not we're adding additional tracking at a certain rate.

450
00:42:06,480 --> 00:42:15,360
Or you could say, if we're wildly successful, we need to evaluate within a month how quickly we can start deploying an internal solution that can offset that.

451
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:22,480
How much of an overlap time that we need, like a month for comparison of the metrics or something to ensure that things you put in worked.

452
00:42:22,880 --> 00:42:24,160
And then turn the old one off.

453
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:27,440
But as long as you have those, then the process is actually pretty easy.

